metacircular-univalent-unison-of-cubically-receptive-stateboxes-lines-13 = cons "## The capstone" (cons "" (cons "Each word imports a lineage, and each completes the others. Petri and Statebox give processes and their composition. Ceptr gives reception through protocols, and the cube gives reception its exact geometry, a boundary filled, and with it the I Ching's changes, the trigrams of dancing in metaphors and Stokes. Unison gives identity by content. Univalence gives identity as equivalence and transport, and with it what Leibniz asked for. Metacircularity puts the system inside what it describes, so that nothing it relies on escapes its own checks. Remove any one and the others cannot stand as they do here: the composition is atomic, one type." (cons "" (cons "Read as one type, the phrase says: processes whose interface is the cube, receiving boundaries and filling them; identified by content and, beyond content, by equivalence of behavior, with the equivalences kept as paths; all sounding together in one store that many participants share under their own names; and the whole system one of those processes, defined and checked in its own language. Every part of the work is an instance. The language is the theory of these processes. The product is every device running the kernel that holds them. The knowledge graph is their record, with edges as constructions. The workflow is the process of the work itself. Any public projection is the unison made visible. The collective superintelligence the work serves is the unison with every participant in it." (cons "" (cons "Every person named at the beginning is essential to this; take any one away and it does not exist, which is why each of them has all of the credit. The respect owed to them is their work held together, given to everyone, and turned toward healing societies. And the work's next step: all of them in one room." nil))))))
